    ("Chile" :region "latin-america" :globe "Latin America" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (75 70 70 72 75 70 75 55) :hofstede (63 23 28 86 31 68) :highlights ("Most formal and structured of LatAm: punctuality is respected, agendas followed, dress conservative." "High uncertainty avoidance: bring documentation, references, guarantees." "Reserved warmth: relationship still decides, but expressed through correctness and repeated contact."))
    ("China" :region "east-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (80 80 80 55 85 80 60 55) :hofstede (80 20 66 30 87 24) :highlights ("Mianzi (face) is the currency: never correct a Chinese counterpart in public, even factually." "Guanxi (relational networks) is the operating system: banquets, favors and intermediaries precede terms." "The contract is the START of the relationship, not its conclusion -- expect renegotiation as circumstances evolve." "'Yes' means 'I hear you', not 'I agree'; 'maybe' and 'it will be difficult' usually mean no." "Hierarchy is steep but decisions are consensual-under-the-boss: the team pre-aligns (the real meeting happens before the meeting)." "Long-term orientation: they will trade short-term margin for long-term position; price patiently." "Gift protocol: give/receive with both hands, modest value (anti-corruption law is strict), never a clock."))
