    ("Denmark" :region "nordic" :globe "Nordic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (40 50 20 30 25 30 15 55) :hofstede (18 74 16 23 35 70) :highlights ("Lowest uncertainty avoidance + low hierarchy: improvise, pilot, iterate -- heavy planning reads as insecurity." "Hygge atmosphere in meetings: informal, humorous, first names, but decisions still go through consensus." "Humour is dry and pervasive; being able to take a joke is a trust signal."))
    ("Egypt" :region "mena" :globe "Middle East" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (85 82 85 85 88 82 85 60) :hofstede (80 25 45 80 7 4) :highlights ("Baksheesh and wasta culture: every process has a human key; tips and intermediaries lubricate." "Extreme high-context: listen for what is unsaid; a direct refusal is almost never spoken." "Politeness is lavish and commitments are soft -- confirm everything in writing, gently, multiple times." "Bargaining is a social ritual with warmth; the first price is an invitation to a conversation."))
    ("Finland" :region "nordic" :globe "Nordic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (45 55 22 30 25 35 15 60) :hofstede (33 63 26 59 38 57) :highlights ("Silence is communication: Finns pause long before answering -- fill it and you lose standing." "Say what you mean, mean what you say: a Finn's 'maybe' is a real maybe, 'yes' is iron." "Sauna invitation is a relationship milestone; declining politely is fine, joining builds deep trust." "Less consensus theatre than Sweden; more quiet personal responsibility."))
    ("France" :region "latin-europe" :globe "Latin Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (70 65 55 70 50 45 55 85) :hofstede (68 71 43 86 63 48) :highlights ("Most principles-first persuaders in the West: method, logic and theory before conclusions -- or you look lightweight." "Debate is intellectually valued; challenging your argument is respect, not attack." "The boss decides (grande ecole hierarchy); build the technical case for the cadre, not the crowd." "Lunch is business: relationship and hierarchy play out over the table, and August is dead month." "Criticism is direct in content, elegant in form; a French 'interesting' often means doubtful."))
    ("Germany" :region "germanic" :globe "Germanic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (25 20 25 40 25 30 10 75) :hofstede (35 67 66 65 83 40) :highlights ("Most low-context communicators in the West: say exactly what you mean; euphemism reads as evasion." "Direct negative feedback is professional, not personal -- do not soften, do not take offence." "Most linear schedulers: the agenda is a contract; being 10 minutes early is on time." "Principles-first: explain the method and the 'why' before the price, or you seem unserious." "Titles and order matter (Dr., Herr/Frau + surname); decisions are slow to form, then immovable." "Separate the person from the problem is NOT the local rule -- criticism lands on the work, but relationships stay formal until you are invited in."))
    ("Greece" :region "latin-europe" :globe "Latin Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (78 72 65 65 70 50 75 65) :hofstede (60 35 57 112 45 50) :highlights ("Highest recorded uncertainty avoidance: reduce risk on paper and in person, repeatedly." "High-context, personal networks (gnosi) open doors that formal channels never will." "Lively interruption = interest; a silent Greek meeting is a failed one."))
    ("Hong Kong" :region "east-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (80 78 78 70 72 78 60 50) :hofstede (68 25 57 29 61 17) :highlights ("Chinese face-and-relationship core wrapped in Anglo deal speed: fastest contracts in the Sinosphere." "Efficient, transactional surface over guanxi foundations -- still relationship-gated underneath." "Cantonese dining etiquette at business banquets; respect seniority ordering at the table."))
    ("Hungary" :region "eastern-europe" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (55 55 55 60 55 50 50 68) :hofstede (46 80 88 82 50 31) :highlights ("Pessimistic-precise communication: problems are stated first and plainly; optimism reads as naivety." "Status-conscious and formal at the table, but proud of technical excellence -- lead with expertise." "High uncertainty avoidance + high masculinity: strong plans, strong egos, hard bargaining."))
    ("India" :region "south-asia" :globe "Southern Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (75 75 82 78 80 75 78 55) :hofstede (77 48 56 40 51 26) :highlights ("Hierarchy decides: deference to the senior person is expected; skip-level pressure causes silent sabotage." "Jugaad (frugal improvisation) mindset: flexibility is a virtue; the plan is a hypothesis." "High-context harmony: a direct 'no' is rare -- 'we'll try', 'should be possible', or head-wobble = polite maybe." "Time is polychronic: meetings start late, are interrupted, and relationships stretch schedules -- but deadlines for YOUR deliverables are enforced hard." "Relationship + family small talk opens everything; food hospitality is generous (respect dietary rules by community)." "Bargaining is a sport: first quotes are anchors; warm persistence beats cold logic."))
    ("Indonesia" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Southeast Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (85 85 85 75 85 85 82 50) :hofstede (78 14 46 48 62 38) :highlights ("Pancasila consensus + musyawarah (deliberation-to-accord): meetings are long, courteous, and the decision emerges from socialization outside the room." "Face (jaga muka) is absolute: never say a hard no; indirect channels carry the real message." "Paternal hierarchy with the Bapak (father/patron) at the center -- the patron's blessing IS the decision." "Patience with time ('jam karet' = rubber time); Ramadan and Lebaran shut business for weeks." "Right hand only for exchange; modest gifts accepted graciously; never show anger -- composure is power."))
    ("Ireland" :region "anglo" :globe "Anglo" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (60 55 30 50 40 45 40 35) :hofstede (28 70 68 35 24 65) :highlights ("Storytelling and humour open meetings; skip the small talk and you seem cold, not efficient." "More relationship-driven than the UK: the pub conversation is part of the deal, not a distraction." "Criticism is wrapped; be careful not to read Irish politeness as full agreement."))
    ("Israel" :region "mena" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (50 35 45 60 45 15 55 50) :hofstede (13 54 47 81 38 37) :highlights ("Dugri (straight talk): interruption, challenge and bluntness are engagement -- the most confrontational debating culture." "Chutzpah is admired; hierarchy is flat in practice (first names with the CEO), informal in dress." "Army-network trust: 'who did you serve with' opens doors; improvisation beats process." "Do not mistake argument for rejection -- the shouting match often ends in a deal and a hug."))
    ("Italy" :region "latin-europe" :globe "Latin Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (75 70 60 65 65 45 70 65) :hofstede (50 76 70 75 61 30) :highlights ("Relationships and bella figura first: who you are and how you present carries the deal." "Flexible time: meetings start late, run long, and interrupt each other -- that is engagement, not chaos." "Formal titles and dress matter at first meeting; warmth and expressiveness build credit." "Northern and southern Italy differ sharply in pacing and formality -- calibrate per city."))
    ("Japan" :region "east-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (90 88 72 25 70 88 15 50) :hofstede (54 46 95 92 88 42) :highlights ("Most consensual deciders on earth: nemawashi (root-binding) pre-aligns everyone -- decisions are slow, execution instant, and a 'decided' thing never reopens." "Extreme high-context: the air between words carries the message; silence after your proposal is processing, not rejection." "Hierarchy is ceremonial and precise: meishi (card) exchange with two hands and a bow; seat order by seniority; never skip the visiting-card ritual." "Indirect refusal vocabulary: 'it is difficult', 'we will consider', silence -- push for a clear yes and you force a face-losing no." "Perfectionism and risk-aversion (world-high UAI): bring exhaustive QC data, references, contingency plans." "Drinking (nomikai) is where the real consensus leaks out; never pour your own drink." "Punctuality is absolute -- arrive 10 minutes early; the agenda is a covenant."))
