    ("Laos" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Southeast Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (88 85 88 85 90 88 88 50) :hofstede (70 20 35 60 45 40) :highlights ("One of the most relationship-first cultures on earth: no meaningful deal without invested personal time -- multiple meals, family inquiries, patience measured in months." "Noy-noy (take it easy) pace: deadlines are aspirations; pushing hard reads as disrespect, not efficiency." "Extreme harmony culture: direct refusal almost never happens; 'yes' = 'I acknowledge', silence or deflection = no. A trusted Lao intermediary is mandatory to decode." "Hierarchy + patronage: the senior official/director's private blessing decides; formal signatures follow informally settled reality." "Face is everything: never criticize publicly, never raise your voice, never force a cornered 'no'." "Baci ceremony and toasts build trust (accept them); monks and wats are honored; heads never touched." "Verbal > written: what the senior person says across the table outweighs the document that follows.") :extrapolated t)
    ("Malaysia" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Southeast Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (80 80 82 75 82 82 78 50) :hofstede (100 26 50 36 41 57) :highlights ("Highest recorded power distance: absolute deference to rank; never bypass or contradict a senior Malay in public." "Bumiputera/Malay-Chinese/Indian business ecosystems each with own norms -- identify which network you're in." "Face and harmony: refusals come as 'boleh cuba' (can try); read commitment levels carefully." "Ramadan pacing, Friday prayers, no left-hand giving; halal dining default."))
