    ("Netherlands" :region "germanic" :globe "Germanic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (20 15 15 35 20 25 20 25) :hofstede (38 80 14 53 44 68) :highlights ("Bluntest feedback culture in the world: Dutch directness is candour, not rudeness -- answer in kind." "Most egalitarian: everyone's view is heard regardless of rank; the junior engineer may shoot down your CTO." "Consensus (poldermodel) makes deciding slow, but implementation is fast and everyone is committed." "Calvinist modesty: splashing wealth or exaggerating marks you as untrustworthy." "Lunch is a sandwich at the desk; don't turn it into a relationship ritual."))
