    ("Philippines" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Southeast Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (80 78 82 78 85 82 80 50) :hofstede (94 32 64 44 27 40) :highlights ("Hiya (shame/face) and utang na loob (debt of gratitude) are the real contract: favors create binding obligations." "Pakikisama (smooth social fit): group harmony decides; the amiable consensus in the room may hide private objections surfaced later through a go-between." "Family-first business: the clan network is the org chart; a family elder's word outranks titles." "Warm, Filipino/English bilingual, US-style directness tolerated more than elsewhere in ASEAN -- but never embarrass anyone publicly." "'Bahala na' fatalism on deadlines: add buffer, follow up personally, keep it light."))
    ("Poland" :region "eastern-europe" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (60 55 55 60 60 45 50 65) :hofstede (68 60 64 93 38 80) :highlights ("Formal hierarchy with hospitality: respect titles, expect warmth once invited past the formality." "High uncertainty avoidance: detailed contracts, contingency clauses, repeated written confirmation." "History made flexibility a survival skill -- Poles improvise around rules while demanding them on paper."))
