    ("Romania" :region "eastern-europe" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (70 68 65 70 65 55 60 68) :hofstede (90 30 42 90 52 20) :highlights ("High power distance, relationship deals: the patron at the top decides; work the trusted introducer." "High-context yes: agreement may mean 'I hear you' -- confirm in writing through the hierarchy." "Hospitality is generous and refusal offends; accept the coffee, the tuica story earns the contract."))
    ("Russia" :region "eastern-europe" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (75 65 75 80 75 55 70 72) :hofstede (93 39 36 95 81 20) :highlights ("Avtoritet rules: the senior person decides and being introduced to the right one is 80% of the deal." "Trust is personal and slow: banquets, toasts and dacha invitations are the real negotiation." "High-context and strategic: what is not said is the message; test statements against interests." "Extreme-range bargaining is normal -- the first price is theatre; anchor and hold with warmth." "Contracts are a snapshot of the balance of power, not a final word; renegotiation is expected when power shifts."))
    ("Saudi Arabia" :region "mena" :globe "Middle East" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (85 80 88 88 90 85 85 60) :hofstede (95 25 60 36 36 16) :highlights ("The senior prince/family decision-maker is the deal; everyone else is a channel to him." "Majlis etiquette: accept dates and cardamom coffee (shake cup to decline refill), right hand only." "Personal trust over paper: multiple visits, family inquiries, and patience are the price of entry." "Never ask about wives, never show sole of shoe, never rush -- time is divine (insha'Allah semantics)." "Contracts flexible by design: terms are the start of a relationship, not its end."))
    ("Singapore" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (75 78 78 70 70 78 55 50) :hofstede (74 20 48 8 72 46) :highlights ("Lowest uncertainty-avoidance culture on earth combined with rule-following precision: quick to try new deals, strict about compliance (fines culture)." "Efficient, low-drama, contract-clean East-West hybrid: the easiest Asian entry point, but relationship depth still decides the big accounts." "Multiracial etiquette: match Malay/Indian/Chinese protocols; halal awareness at meals is basic respect." "Kiasu (fear of losing out) drives sharp bargaining; decisions are pragmatic and fast by consensus of a small top team."))
    ("South Africa" :region "subsaharan-africa" :globe "Sub-Saharan Africa" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (60 55 55 60 55 55 50 50) :hofstede (49 65 63 49 34 63) :highlights ("Two business cultures in one country: corporate English-speaking SA is Anglo-linear; township and traditional sectors are relationship-first and communal -- read which room you are in." "Ubuntu reconciliation etiquette: consult broadly, acknowledge history, never dismiss elders." "Direct-ish but diplomatic; braai (barbecue) invitations are the relationship engine." "Load-shedding realism: build schedule slack; patience with infrastructure is a professional skill."))
    ("South Korea" :region "east-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (85 82 82 65 75 85 50 55) :hofstede (60 18 39 85 100 29) :highlights ("Fastest-moving Confucian culture: ppali-ppali (hurry-hurry) pace inside a steep hierarchy -- decisions come quicker than Japan, with less consensus depth." "Kibun (mood/face) management: keep the atmosphere harmonious; causing a senior to lose face is fatal." "Titles and hierarchy are rigid: two-handed card exchange, senior speaks first, drinking rituals (never pour your own glass, turn away when drinking before elders)." "Longest-term orientation recorded: they will lose money for years to own a market." "'We will review it' often means no; use a trusted intermediary to extract the real answer."))
    ("Spain" :region "latin-europe" :globe "Latin Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (75 70 60 60 65 50 72 60) :hofstede (57 51 42 86 48 44) :highlights ("Personal relationship is the deal's engine: invest in sobremesa (the long table conversation after lunch)." "Hierarchy with a human face: the senior person decides, but charm opens the door." "Scheduling is flexible and late dinner is a business arena; August and Christmas week are dead." "Face-saving matters -- criticize privately, never across the table."))
    ("Sri Lanka" :region "south-asia" :globe "Southern Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (80 75 82 80 85 78 82 55) :hofstede (80 35 10 45 nil nil) :highlights ("Ayubowan warmth with formal British-era manners: titles (Mr/Mrs) until invited otherwise." "Buddhist patience culture: unhurried meetings, indirect disagreement, gentle humor." "Hierarchy and family networks decide; Religious festivals (poya days) pause business monthly."))
    ("Sweden" :region "nordic" :globe "Nordic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (40 50 15 25 25 30 15 55) :hofstede (31 71 5 29 53 78) :highlights ("Extreme consensus (samforstand): decisions take many meetings but are then bulletproof -- never force a vote early." "Flat hierarchy: the boss is a coordinator, not a commander; address everyone as equal." "Modesty law (Jantelagen): never claim to be better than the group; credit the team." "Work-life boundary is sacred: schedule meetings inside 9-4, never Friday afternoon; July is out." "Silence is comfort, not awkwardness; pause before answering shows respect."))
    ("Switzerland" :region "germanic" :globe "Germanic Europe" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (25 30 30 40 25 35 10 70) :hofstede (34 68 70 58 74 56) :highlights ("Punctuality is a moral value; late = disrespect, call ahead the moment you know." "Consensus across stakeholders before any announcement -- surprise is a breach of process." "Modest, precise, understated: exaggeration destroys credibility instantly." "German/French/Italian cantons differ; match language and style to the region."))
    ("Taiwan" :region "east-asia" :globe "Confucian Asia" :lewis "reactive" :meyer (82 80 80 65 78 80 60 52) :hofstede (58 17 45 69 93 49) :highlights ("Softer, more indirect than mainland China: extra politeness layers, slower trust, deeper loyalty once won." "Consensus plus hierarchy: the boss decides after quiet alignment; give face to every senior person present." "Night-market banquet culture; gifting modest and gracious. Never discuss cross-strait politics."))
    ("Thailand" :region "southeast-asia" :globe "Southeast Asia" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (85 85 85 80 88 85 82 50) :hofstede (64 20 34 64 32 45) :highlights ("Kreng jai (considerate deference) silences disagreement: a Thai team will warmly agree in the room and quietly not comply after -- verify through allies, not confrontation." "Hierarchy with the boss as khun po (father figure): the senior person's nod matters more than the meeting's consensus." "Sanuk (fun) belongs in work: meetings with warmth and lightness outperform formal pressure." "Face protection: never lose your temper -- visible anger marks YOU, not them, as the problem." "Wai greeting etiquette (press palms, slight bow) by seniority; never touch heads, never point feet." "Monarchy is sacred ground: zero jokes, zero commentary, zero exceptions (lese-majeste is enforced)." "'Up to you' often means 'please decide so no Thai has to refuse you'."))
    ("Turkey" :region "mena" :globe "Eastern Europe" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (80 78 75 78 80 70 78 65) :hofstede (66 37 45 85 46 49) :highlights ("Relationship-first: tea, meals and long personal talk precede business; rushing reads as disrespect." "Hierarchical and status-aware: meet the decision-maker, honor the pecking order, dress well." "Hospitality is a moral code -- praise the tea, never criticize Turkey, and expect vigorous, friendly bargaining." "'Insallah' framing on commitments: distinguish enthusiasm from a dated, owned promise."))
    ("United Arab Emirates" :region "mena" :globe "Middle East" :lewis "multi-active" :meyer (85 80 85 85 88 80 80 60) :hofstede (90 36 50 66 nil nil) :highlights ("Wasta (connections) is infrastructure: the right Emirati sponsor or introducer changes everything." "Majlis protocol: coffee and extended courtesy talk open the meeting; never rush to the pitch." "Face is non-negotiable -- a direct 'no' is rare; 'leave it with me' may be a polite refusal." "Friday-Saturday weekend; Ramadan working hours shrink and eating in public by day is banned." "Haggling is expected on almost everything except listed corporate rates; anchor high, concede slowly, keep warm."))
    ("United Kingdom" :region "anglo" :globe "Anglo" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (60 55 30 55 30 40 35 25) :hofstede (35 89 66 35 51 69) :highlights ("High-context irony and understatement: 'quite good' may mean excellent; 'a bit of a problem' may mean disaster." "Indirect negative feedback via British humour and euphemism -- decode the joke before responding literally." "Email formality: open with small talk, avoid first names until offered, sign off politely." "Class and school ties still lubricate trust; a shared alma mater beats a sharp pitch." "Decisions drift through meetings-before-the-meeting; the room rarely surprises the principals."))
    ("United States" :region "anglo" :globe "Anglo" :lewis "linear-active" :meyer (55 45 25 60 25 30 30 15) :hofstede (40 91 62 46 26 68) :highlights ("Trust is task-based: competence, punctual delivery and follow-through build credit faster than dinners." "'How are you?' is a greeting, not a question; 'let's do lunch' is a friendly close, not always an invite." "Get to the point fast: conclusion first, then support (most applications-first culture on earth)." "Positive framing expected: package criticism as 'opportunities'; blunt negativity reads as hostility." "Decisions come fast and are revisited just as fast -- a signed agreement can be reopened by a new VP." "Litigation mindset: the written contract is the relationship's boundary."))
