  "The countries covered, by canonical name.")

(defparameter *regions*
  '(
    ("anglo" :label "Anglo (US, Canada, UK, Ireland, Australia, New Zealand)" :trust "Task-based: track record, contracts, punctual delivery. Trust grows through demonstrated competence and reliability; two strong deliveries beat five dinners." :decision "Fast, individual accountability: an empowered manager decides in the meeting; decisions can be reopened when circumstances change." :communication "Low-to-mid context: say what you mean, email is direct, humor softens but does not obscure." :contract "The written contract is the deal. Deviations are negotiated as formal amendments." :etiquette ("Punctuality matters (5-10 min early in North America; slightly looser in Ireland)" "First names common fast in US/CA/AU/NZ; wait a beat in UK/IE formal settings" "Modest gifts only, and only after a deal or at holidays (policy limits in corporates)" "Small talk: sport, weather, travel -- avoid politics/religion at first meeting") :taboos ("Overselling or exaggerated claims (instant credibility loss)" "Confusing Canada with the US, or Australia with New Zealand" "Assuming London slang/irony translates literally"))
    ("east-asia" :label "East Asia (China, Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, Hong Kong)" :trust "Relationship-based: banquets, favors, time invested. Guanxi/kankei networks are the operating system -- a warm introduction is worth a year of cold outreach." :decision "Consensus beneath hierarchy: nemawashi/ringi (Japan) pre-aligns silently; China pre-aligns before the meeting; the senior person ratifies. Slow yes, fast execution, never reopened." :communication "High context: what is NOT said carries the message. 'It is difficult' = no. Silence = processing. Save face for everyone, always." :contract "The contract BEGINS the relationship (China: renegotiable as circumstances evolve; Japan: near-absolute once sealed)." :etiquette ("Business cards with two hands, read respectfully, laid out by seating (Japan/Korea)" "Banquet seating by seniority; toast the senior counterpart first; never pour your own drink" "Modest, thoughtful gifts given/received with two hands (mind anti-corruption law in China)" "Punctuality absolute in Japan; keep agendas tight everywhere") :taboos ("Public correction or causing loss of face (mianzi/kibun) -- fatal and remembered" "Forcing a direct 'no' or pushing for a fast decision" "White/black gift wrapping, clocks, or anything with unlucky number 4 (China)" "Political small talk (cross-strait, Korea-Japan history, CCP topics)"))
    ("eastern-europe" :label "Eastern Europe (Poland, Czechia, Hungary, Romania, Russia)" :trust "Personal and guarded at first: proven loyalty over time. Hospitality is generous once you're inside; skepticism is the default outside." :decision "Top-down: the director/owner decides; formal hierarchy respected. Implementation bends around reality (improvisation is a survival skill)." :communication "Mid-high context with direct edges: pessimism-first framing, irony, reading what's unsaid. Russians negotiate in wide ranges strategically." :contract "Treated as a power snapshot: signed, but renegotiated when leverage or circumstances shift. Detail and contingencies still expected on paper." :etiquette ("Formal titles and surnames at first; flowers/odd-number customs if invited home" "Vodka toasts (Russia, Poland) -- pace yourself, never refuse the first" "Bring documents, certificates, stamps: paperwork confers legitimacy" "Strong tea/coffee hospitality -- always accept") :taboos ("Disrespecting seniority or skipping the hierarchy" "Treating signed paper as final protection without relationship maintenance" "Comparing the country unfavorably to 'the West'"))
    ("germanic" :label "Germanic Europe (Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Netherlands)" :trust "Task-based and evidence-based: credentials, precision, documented competence. Overpromising is the cardinal sin." :decision "Structured and deliberate: analysis first, decision once, then rigid execution. Consensus in NL/CH slows the front end and accelerates the back end." :communication "Low context, direct negative feedback: criticism of the work is normal and expected; soften it yourself, don't expect them to." :contract "Near-sacred: what is signed happens, exactly as written. Compliance and process rigor are trust signals." :etiquette ("Punctuality is respect (early is on time)" "Titles (Dr., Prof.) in D/A/CH until offered otherwise" "Agendas are contracts; keep to them and send follow-ups in writing" "Separate business meals are functional, not relationship theaters (esp. NL)") :taboos ("Hype, adjectives, and salesmanship" "Surprise changes to a settled plan or agenda" "Casual dress or chummy first-naming at first meetings (D/A/CH)"))
    ("latin-america" :label "Latin America (Mexico, Brazil, Argentina, Chile, Colombia, Peru)" :trust "Personalismo: the person IS the deal. Warmth, simpatia, family references, and shared meals build the confidence that paper only records." :decision "Hierarchical with staged consensus: the patrao/dueno decides; meetings build the feeling of agreement that the boss ratifies." :communication "High context, emotionally expressive: harmony-preserving ('yes' to be polite), indirect criticism, loud friendly interruption = interest." :contract "Framework for the relationship: details flex; renegotiation is normal; personal commitment enforces more than clauses." :etiquette ("Stand-up greetings, firm handshake, sustained eye contact, closer personal distance" "Titles (Licenciado, Ingeniero, Don/Dona) and formal usted until invited" "Long business lunches/dinners are the real negotiation arena" "Accept hospitality enthusiastically; modest gratitude gifts appreciated") :taboos ("Cold, brusque, all-business demeanor" "Public embarrassment or confrontational feedback" "Assuming LatAm is one market (Chile != Brazil != Mexico)" "US-centric comparisons or arrogance about 'efficiency'"))
    ("latin-europe" :label "Latin Europe (France, Belgium, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Greece)" :trust "Mixed: personal rapport opens doors, intellectual respect sustains them. Eloquence and form matter as much as content." :decision "Hierarchical with consultation: the senior cadre/patron decides; the path runs through formal channels dressed in personal relationships." :communication "Mid-to-high context, rhetorically rich: theory and method before conclusion (esp. France); interruption signals engagement (esp. Italy, Greece)." :contract "Important but treated as a living framework; terms get revisited as relationships and realities evolve." :etiquette ("Titles and vous/Lei formality until invited" "Business lunches are real work (1.5-2h); dinner invitations are a trust milestone" "Dress well -- appearance signals respect for the counterpart" "August vacations and regional holidays blank out decision-making") :taboos ("Jumping to price before establishing the intellectual frame" "Public criticism or losing your composure" "Treating a heated debate as hostility"))
    ("mena" :label "Middle East & North Africa (UAE, Saudi, Egypt, Turkey, Israel*)" :trust "Relationship-based: majlis/coffee hospitality, extended courtesy talk, family reputation. Wasta (intercession networks) is infrastructure." :decision "Top-down via the senior male/patron: the decision-maker's private blessing is the decision; formal process follows informally settled reality." :communication "High context with lavish politeness: direct refusal almost never spoken; 'insha'Allah' separates intent from dated commitment (Israel is the outlier: dugri directness)." :contract "Start of a relationship: terms flex as the relationship and power balance evolve; personal guarantee outranks corporate paper." :etiquette ("Right hand only for giving/receiving/eating" "Accept coffee/dates; shake the tiny cup to decline refill; praise the hospitality" "Dress conservatively; meetings may be interrupted by phone/visitors -- flow with it" "Ramadan: no public eating/drinking by day, shortened hours; Friday-Saturday weekend (Gulf)" "Never ask about wives/female family members") :taboos ("Rushing the pitch before courtesy rituals complete" "Public loss of face, criticism, or showing anger" "Alcohol/pork gifting; sole of shoe displayed toward anyone" "Middle East politics, religion debates, or Israel/Arab conflations"))
    ("nordic" :label "Nordic Europe (Sweden, Norway, Denmark, Finland)" :trust "Task-based with flat-hierarchy candor: honesty, modesty, consistency. Trust is high at start and lost by misbehavior." :decision "Consensus-first (esp. Sweden): many consultations, one durable decision; the boss facilitates rather than commands." :communication "Low-mid context, restrained: say it plainly, pause before answering, silence is comfortable. Modesty law: never claim superiority." :contract "Reliable and simple: honest terms, honest execution; disputes are rare and handled plainly." :etiquette ("Flat dress code, first names immediately, minimal titles" "Respect 9-to-4 meeting windows; never Friday afternoon; July and Christmas are walls" "Lunch is short; the real relationship ritual is the cabin/sauna/ski invitation" "Credit the group, never yourself") :taboos ("Self-aggrandizement or flashing wealth/status" "Pressing for a decision before consensus forms" "Overfamiliarity or aggressive persuasion techniques"))
    ("south-asia" :label "South Asia (India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka)" :trust "Relationship-based with family-network roots: personal trust, hospitality exchanged, introducers vouched. Family firm patriarchs own decisions." :decision "Steeply hierarchical: deference to seniors expected; decisions concentrated at the top, executed with jugaad flexibility below." :communication "High context, harmony-preserving: no direct 'no'; head-wobble (India) = polite non-commitment; enthusiasm != commitment." :contract "Negotiable instrument: bargaining is a sport, timelines are elastic, renegotiation normal. Your deadlines will be enforced harder than theirs." :etiquette ("Ask about family/health (avoid asking about wives directly in PK/BD)" "Respect dietary codes by community (vegetarian, halal, no beef)" "Titles matter (Dr./Engineer/Sir); wait for first-name permission" "Tea/coffee and snacks always accepted; festival calendars (Diwali, Eid) pause business") :taboos ("Left hand for giving/receiving; feet/shoes pointing at people" "Skip-level pressure or bypassing the senior decision-maker" "Cold, purely transactional approach without a warm introducer"))
    ("southeast-asia" :label "Southeast Asia (ASEAN: Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Thailand, Vietnam, Philippines, Laos, Cambodia, Myanmar)" :trust "Relationship-based to the extreme: meals, family inquiries, patient time. Deals move at the speed of personal confidence, not paper." :decision "Hierarchical with consensus performance: the senior director/patron decides privately; meetings ratify what was already socialized. Verbal signals from the senior person outweigh written process." :communication "High context, harmony-preserving: 'yes' means 'I hear you'; refusals arrive as silence, deflection, or 'we will try'. Kreng jai (TH), anade (MM), hiya (PH) all suppress open disagreement." :contract "A written snapshot of a relationship: useful for alignment, but reality is renegotiated verbally as circumstances change. Keep warm contact between formal milestones." :etiquette ("Wai/sompeah greetings by seniority; never touch heads, never point feet (TH/KH/LA/MM)" "Right hand or both hands for giving/receiving; remove shoes when entering homes/offices" "Halal awareness (MY/ID): no alcohol at Malay/Muslim meals; Ramadan hours respected" "Accept tea and hospitality always; decline graciously only with a reason" "Monarchy (TH) and religion (monks, wats, pagodas) are sacred -- zero jokes") :taboos ("Displaying anger or impatience -- it marks YOU as untrustworthy" "Public criticism or forcing a face-losing admission" "Rushing to contract before the relationship is cooked" "Assuming ASEAN is one culture: Singapore != Indonesia != Laos"))
    ("subsaharan-africa" :label "Sub-Saharan Africa (Nigeria, Kenya, South Africa*)" :trust "Relationship-communal: extended greetings and family inquiries ARE the meeting; networks (clan, church, community) decide what org charts only record." :decision "Elders and hierarchy first, then communal consultation: the senior person opens and closes; ubuntu consensus legitimizes implementation." :communication "High context, warm, indirect on refusal: a soft answer often hides a hard no; read intermediaries and body language." :contract "Important but relationship-negotiated: personal commitment and follow-up visits sustain terms paper alone cannot enforce." :etiquette ("Greet EVERYONE in seniority order, handshake with two hands or right hand + left-hand touch for elders" "Titles are mandatory (Chief, Doctor, Engineer, Pastor) -- never first-name a senior" "Accept hospitality generously; small thoughtful gifts honor the relationship (never bribes)" "Time is event-based: meetings start when relationships are ready; build schedule slack") :taboos ("Skipping the greeting ritual to 'get to business'" "Disrespecting elders or community structures" "Left-hand exchanges; public correction of a senior person")))
  "The regional playbooks a country's brief is built on, by region key.")
